    "_comment": "Unary elementwise-activation family (CK Tile 21_elementwise parity). op_kind is the honest node type 'pointwise'; the ActivationAdapter accepts only the unary-activation subset and encodes which op via the decoded 'activation' token (silu <- SWISH_FWD beta==1; gelu_tanh <- GELU_APPROX_TANH_FWD), so each kernel constrains dtype+activation and every variant serves any numel {min:1} (the kernel's scalar tail handles the ragged remainder, so no multiple_of is needed). block_size/vec are perf-only; the grid is ceil_div(numel, block_size*vec). Exact erf GELU is declined by the adapter (no builder op yet) -- a documented follow-up.",
